ABSTRACT
The rapid growth of urban populations has increased the demand for efficient, transparent, and accessible municipal services. However, many local government services remain fragmented across multiple platforms, making it difficult for citizens to register complaints, monitor service requests, or access government welfare schemes efficiently.
NagarSathi is a smart citizen service platform designed to simplify communication between citizens and municipal authorities through a unified digital interface. The platform enables users to register complaints, track complaint status, explore government schemes, interact with an AI-powered municipal assistant, access emergency contacts, and monitor municipal updates through an interactive dashboard.
The application has been developed using HTML5, CSS3, and JavaScript while utilizing browser technologies such as Web Speech API, Speech Recognition API, Local Storage API, Fetch API, and FileReader API. The platform is responsive, multilingual, and user-friendly, ensuring accessibility across various devices.
Although the current implementation is a frontend prototype, the modular architecture allows future integration with databases, authentication systems, GPS-based complaint reporting, AI-powered image analysis, multilingual support, and mobile applications.
