CHAPTER 1
INTRODUCTION
Digital governance has become an essential requirement for modern smart cities. Citizens expect government services to be transparent, easily accessible, and available online. Traditional municipal systems often require physical visits to government offices, increasing delays and reducing citizen engagement.
NagarSathi is a web-based smart citizen platform that centralizes multiple municipal services into a single application. It provides citizens with an easy-to-use interface for complaint registration, complaint tracking, AI-assisted support, government schemes, emergency contacts, and municipal information.
The project demonstrates how modern frontend web technologies can contribute to improving digital governance while providing an intuitive and responsive user experience.
CHAPTER 2
PROBLEM STATEMENT
Current municipal systems face several challenges, including:
• Fragmented online services
• Manual complaint registration
• Lack of complaint tracking
• Poor transparency
• Limited awareness of government welfare schemes
• Language barriers
• Limited digital accessibility
These issues reduce citizen participation and create unnecessary administrative workload.
CHAPTER 3
OBJECTIVES
The primary objectives of NagarSathi are:
• Develop a centralized municipal service portal.
• Simplify complaint registration.
• Improve complaint tracking.
• Increase transparency between citizens and municipal authorities.
• Provide easy access to government welfare schemes.
• Integrate AI-based citizen assistance.
• Support multilingual interaction.
• Provide responsive web accessibility.
CHAPTER 4
PROPOSED SOLUTION
NagarSathi provides a unified web platform that combines multiple municipal services into a single application.
The platform enables citizens to:
• Register complaints
• Upload issue photographs
• Track complaint status
• Explore government welfare schemes
• Access municipal services
• Interact with an AI chatbot
• Use voice-based interaction
• View municipal dashboard information
• Access emergency contacts
The proposed system focuses on improving accessibility, transparency, and citizen engagement through an intuitive interface.
